  "description": "Change of use from Class E (Office) to Class Sui Generis (Large HMO) to provide 12 rooms, involving erection of a part one, part two storey rear extension, provision of light well, alterations to the fenestrations, refuse store to the rear and internal cycle store.\r",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The submitted Parking Stress Survey confirms that the surrounding highway network is already operating at a critical saturation level of 85%. Consequently, the development would lead to an unacceptable increase in on-street parking demand and overspill onto unrestricted residential side streets where no surplus capacity exists. This would result in distinct harm to the functional integrity of the highway and compromise local road safety.\r\r The proposal is therefore contrary to policies 36 and 37 of the Sutton Local Plan (2018) and Policies T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (2021)."
  ],
